<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<figure xml:id="cat-c02-fig-universal">
  <caption>The two factorization conditions: from <m>X</m> to <m>F</m> on the left, and from <m>F</m> to <m>X</m> on the right.</caption>
  <image xml:id="cat-c02-image-universal" width="72%">
    <latex-image>
\begin{tikzcd}[row sep=large, column sep=large]
  X \arrow[r, "u"] \arrow[dr, "v"'] \amp
  F(A) \arrow[d, dashed, "F(a)"] \\
  \amp F(B)
\end{tikzcd}
\qquad
\begin{tikzcd}[row sep=large, column sep=large]
  F(A) \arrow[r, "u"] \amp X \\
  F(B) \arrow[u, dashed, "F(a)"] \arrow[ur, "v"'] \amp
\end{tikzcd}
    </latex-image>
    <description><p>Two commutative triangles. On the left, v from X to F(B) factors as u from X to F(A) followed by the uniquely induced F(a). On the right, v from F(B) to X factors through the uniquely induced F(a) to F(A), followed by u. The induced arrows are dashed.</p></description>
  </image>
</figure>